# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MERNIUM — server-side email settings for /api/enquiry
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development (`npm run dev`)
# and add the same variables in Vercel:
#   Project → Settings → Environment Variables (Production + Preview)
#
# These are read ONLY by the serverless function. Never prefix them
# with VITE_ — that would bundle them into the public website.
# Enquiries are always delivered to mernium.learn@gmail.com.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Option A (recommended for a Gmail inbox): Gmail SMTP with an App Password
#   1. Sign in to mernium.learn@gmail.com → Google Account → Security.
#   2. Turn on 2-Step Verification (required for App Passwords).
#   3. Security → App passwords → create one named "MERNIUM website".
#   4. Paste the 16-character password below WITHOUT spaces.
#   Gmail only sends "From" the signed-in account (or verified aliases),
#   so MAIL_FROM must use mernium.learn@gmail.com.
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=465
SMTP_SECURE=true
SMTP_USER=mernium.learn@gmail.com
SMTP_PASS=your-16-character-app-password
MAIL_FROM="MERNIUM <mernium.learn@gmail.com>"

# Option B: a transactional provider with SMTP (Brevo, Resend, SendGrid, Postmark…)
#   Use the provider's SMTP host/port/username/API key, and set MAIL_FROM to a
#   sender address or domain you have VERIFIED with that provider, e.g.
#   MAIL_FROM="MERNIUM <hello@your-verified-domain.com>"
#   Replies still go to the student (internal email) and to
#   mernium.learn@gmail.com (acknowledgement) via Reply-To.

# Notes
# - Gmail personal accounts allow roughly 500 messages/day; each enquiry sends 2.
# - Rate limiting (5 submissions per IP per 10 minutes) and duplicate protection
#   run in memory per serverless instance. For stricter limits across all
#   instances, add a shared store such as Vercel KV / Upstash Redis.
